            <note corresp="#d304-f2" n="1" xml:id="d304-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f3" n="2" xml:id="d304-f3-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg445">p. 445</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f4" n="3" xml:id="d304-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram 2223, June 14, to London, not printed, instructed the Embassy in London
                    to ask the British to deny overflight rights of its zone of occupation in
                    Germany to Yugoslavia which had requested such rights for weekly flights between
                    Belgrade and Amsterdam (856.79660h/6–1448).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d304-f5" n="4" xml:id="d304-f5-content">
                <p>J. Paul Barringer, Deputy Director, Office of Transportation and Communications,
                    Department of State, served as Vice Chairman of the United States Delegation to
                    the Second Annual Assembly of the International Civil Aviation Organization,
                    held in Geneva, June 1–22, 1948.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
